# Force HTTPS: instruct browsers to only ever connect over TLS (mirrors the
# marketing site). The HTTP→HTTPS redirect itself is the Cloudflare zone
# "Always Use HTTPS" setting.
#
# Content-Security-Policy (2026-10-12), enforced. What the app really reaches
# for, and nothing else (the same recipe as Universal PDF):
#   • script-src: its own bundle; the inline pre-paint theme script in
#     index.html, by its sha256 (scripts/theme.test.mjs fails if the script
#     changes without this hash following); MediaPipe's WASM loader
#     for "Blur faces", from its pinned jsDelivr folder (src/lib/faceBlur.ts);
#     blob: for the module the ONNX runtime behind "Remove background" builds
#     and imports at run time.
#     'wasm-unsafe-eval' for the WebAssembly in background removal, face
#     detection and the HEIC decoder. 'unsafe-eval' because background
#     removal's ndarray and the HEIC decoder's Emscripten bindings build
#     functions at run time; it does not let any other origin's script in.
#     No 'unsafe-inline'.
#   • style-src 'unsafe-inline': React style attributes, everywhere.
#   • connect-src: Supabase (the SDK's client; no sign-in since 2026-10-20,
#     `noAccounts` in src/main.tsx), the suite changelog, and the two AI
#     model downloads — background removal's model and runtime
#     (staticimgly.com) and the face detector's runtime (jsDelivr) and model
#     (Google's model storage). Pictures never go to any of them.
#   • worker-src 'self' blob:: the image workers, the service worker, and the
#     AI runtimes' blob: workers.
#   • img-src https:: avatars come from anywhere a user points.
#   • No Cloudflare Web Analytics. Cloudflare's zone-level automatic setup
#     injects its beacon (static.cloudflareinsights.com) into the live HTML;
#     script-src does not allow it, so it never runs. Turn the injection off for
#     this host in Cloudflare (Web Analytics site rules) to stop the refused
#     request showing in the console.
# The dev server serves the same policy Report-Only (vite.config.ts, cspDev()).
#
# Hardening. Nothing in the suite frames this app, so refusing to be framed
# elsewhere costs nothing and closes off click-jacking.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' blob: 'unsafe-eval' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'sha256-J6EIRN5aZTJK+dDLx2Ffx8Mvt+eVCVvObQFpJiUvlOI=' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@mediapipe/; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; font-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' data: blob: https://rygfxgalojojppxmhddo.supabase.co wss://rygfxgalojojppxmhddo.supabase.co https://changelog.unisim.co.uk https://staticimgly.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@mediapipe/ https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self' blob:; media-src 'self' blob: data:; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'
